/** @mainpage Qore mongodb Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section mongodbintro mongodb Module Introduction

    <img src="mongodb-logo.svg" width="96" alt="mongodb module logo"/>

    The \c mongodb module provides MongoDB database connectivity for %Qore programs, allowing
    applications to interact with MongoDB servers for document storage, retrieval, and management.

    This module wraps the libmongoc C driver library to provide efficient and full-featured
    MongoDB connectivity including:
    - Connection management with connection pooling
    - CRUD operations (Create, Read, Update, Delete)
    - Aggregation pipelines
    - Cursor-based iteration for large result sets
    - BSON type support including ObjectId

    A call that waits for the server (connecting, the TLS handshake, reading or writing) ends as soon as the thread is
    cancelled (@ref Qore::cancel_thread() "cancel_thread()") or its @ref Qore::Program "Program" is interrupted
    (@ref Qore::SandboxManager::requestInterrupt() "SandboxManager::requestInterrupt()"), and so does the conversion
    of a large list to BSON.  A hash or list nested too deeply to be converted to BSON, or a BSON document nested too
    deeply to be converted to a hash, raises \c STACK-LIMIT-EXCEEDED.

    A document received from the server is converted to a hash with its strings (string values, code, symbols,
    regular expressions and their options, DBPointer collections) tagged UTF-8 and its keys converted to the default
    encoding (the encoding of hash keys, as \c parse_json() converts its keys); a BSON string or key that is not valid
    UTF-8 (which libbson does not check in the documents that it reads, and which a document written by another driver
    or an older server can have) raises \c INVALID-ENCODING with the byte offset of the first invalid byte sequence,
    as does a database or collection name from the server that is not valid UTF-8.

    Text given to the driver is UTF-8: the strings of a document are converted to UTF-8 and its keys from the default
    encoding, and the URI and the database and collection names given to the module are checked in their encodings
    (\c INVALID-ENCODING) and converted to UTF-8; the names returned by \c getName() are tagged UTF-8.  A document
    with a key that the default encoding cannot hold (ex: \c "€" with an \c ISO-8859-1 default encoding) raises
    \c ENCODING-CONVERSION-ERROR where it is converted to a hash.

    This module is released under the MIT license (see \c COPYING.MIT in the source distribution for
    more information). The module is tagged as such in the module's header (meaning it can be loaded
    unconditionally regardless of how the %Qore library was initialized).

    To use the module in a %Qore script, use the \c %%requires directive as follows:
    @code{.py} %requires mongodb @endcode

    Classes provided by this module:
    - @ref mongodb::MongoClient "MongoClient" - MongoDB client connection management
    - @ref mongodb::MongoDatabase "MongoDatabase" - MongoDB database operations
    - @ref mongodb::MongoCollection "MongoCollection" - MongoDB collection CRUD operations
    - <tt>MongoCursor&lt;DocT&gt;</tt> - Cursor for iterating query results
    - @ref mongodb::ObjectId "ObjectId" - MongoDB ObjectId type

